<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29876" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multīcĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj.,
				soft, splendid, transparent</i>, a term applied to garments
				(<b>poet.</b> and post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: dabis Aureliano tunicas multicias viriles
			decem (al. multilicias), Valerian. Aug. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Vop. Aurel. 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">synthesis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. de Pall. 4</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multīcĭa</span></b> ,
			ōrum, n., sc. vestimenta, <i>soft, splendid, transparent garments</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 2,
			66</span></i>; <i><span class="en">76</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 186</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
